IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS:

1. Configure the correct base URL and navigate directly to CountryPass.html. There is no login step.
2. Inspect the actual DOM and use verified element IDs, accessible labels, or reliable locators.
3. Implement a CountryPassPage class with reusable methods for every form field and submission.
4. Implement at least 15 meaningful automated test methods. Helper methods do not count as test methods.
5. Include positive, negative, boundary, required-field, dropdown, radio-button, checkbox, textarea, and complete-submission scenarios.
6. Map test coverage to all 14 user stories.
7. Assert observable behavior: field values, selections, validation messages, submission results, or confirmation details.
8. Respect the documented validation rules. Do not expect email, number, or date-format validation unless supported by the requirements and actual application.
9. Do not invent element IDs, messages, dropdown values, or successful outcomes.
10. Keep tests isolated and repeatable. Use suitable waits and avoid arbitrary sleeps, brittle selectors, unnecessary force clicks, and duplicated code.
11. Do not hard-code a validation message without confirming it.
12. Configure useful HTML reporting and include commands for installing dependencies, installing Playwright browsers, running tests, running headed tests, and generating reports.
13. Use the Playwright version compatible with the installed environment.
14. Generate complete source files, not partial snippets.
15. If browser execution is available, install dependencies, compile TypeScript, run the tests, and fix genuine errors.
16. Never remove valid tests or weaken assertions simply to make the report green.
17. Do not claim tests passed unless they actually ran and passed.

Before finishing, verify that the project structure, imports, selectors, configuration, and execution instructions are consistent. Explain which commands I need to run.
